  "knownDifferences": [
    "GeoMoose dispatches one identify action across visible template-capable layers; OpenGeo fans out separately authorized, generation-aware requests across each unique visible governed dataset and reports per-layer failures.",
    "GeoMoose applies a map-resolution-dependent point tolerance; OpenGeo exposes Point, MultiPoint, LineString, Polygon, two-corner Box, and Modify selection tools with an explicit meter buffer.",
    "GeoMoose promotes current result features directly into its buffer-select service; OpenGeo copies no more than 100 exact result geometries with source dataset, generation, query digest, and stable feature identifiers before the user adds them to a target dataset query.",
    "GeoMoose CSV uses configured grid columns without an intrinsic row, field, or byte cap; OpenGeo exports deterministic identifiers and safe fields with 100-row, 64-field, and 262144-byte limits plus spreadsheet-formula neutralization."
  ]
